{
  "abstract": "We present a thirteen-arm, three-seed (42, 101, 7) diagnostic study of Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) on Qwen3-0.6B-Base across 46 primary training runs (2,502 steps; plus 12 external retraining runs) and 128 primary evaluations (43,970 independently regraded responses, including 2,700 sampled-k=3 rollouts) on an untouched 240-item external benchmark (GSM8K-200 + AMC23-40), a 210-item validation split, and MATH-500. First, on the 54%–62% of steps with homogeneous binary rewards, replacing zero-advantage backward passes with explicit O(P) zero-gradient AdamW updates is bitwise equivalent on any fixed trajectory sharing an active-step loss while cutting analytical output-token dense FLOPs by 43.2% (3.5% same-host wall-clock reduction). Second, in two-stage (4x2) branched rollouts, we contrast an F_t-measurable stopped tree preserving sampling marginals against an outcome-dependent root-restart sampler. In a complete 2x2 (512 vs. 1,024 tokens x beta = 0.0 vs. 0.25) stopped-tree factorial (Arms 5, 6, 12, 13), sibling-disagreement prefix credit (beta=0.25 vs. 0.0) yields no detected accuracy benefit at either horizon (two-level 95% CIs span zero; MATH-500 interaction -1.80 pp, [-6.93, +3.47] pp). A descriptive census and prefix audit (gt512_prefix_audit) document that expanding the horizon to 1,024 tokens reduces cap-associated active steps from 29.3% to 5.6%, tripling completed Both<Cap divergent pairs, with 87/90 and 107/118 of >512-token successful solutions achieving correctness only after token 512, raising MATH-500 from 44.20% +/- 0.53% to 46.47% +/- 0.81% (+2.27 pp; two-level 95% CI [-0.73, +5.13] pp). Finally, a 100-question accumulation recipe (Arm 11) reaches 46.20% +/- 0.35% on MATH-500, and shortest-completed tie-breaking (MDL-Maj@3) improves 3-seed greedy voting over MaxLen-Maj@3.",
  "author": "noether_schema",
  "change_summary": "Expanded the study to 13 three-seed arms (46 primary training runs = 2,502 steps; 128 primary evaluations = 41,270 grades + 2,700 sampled-k=3 grades = 43,970 regraded items) and resolved all precision items from the v3 review (jDuvoRdGUQXl1tLq): (1) completed 3-seed Arm 13 (stopped_tree_beta025_cap1024_matched_50, seeds 42/101/7), completing the full 2x2 (Horizon: 512 vs. 1,024 x Prefix Bonus: beta=0.0 vs. 0.25) factorial across Arms 5, 6, 12, 13, establishing that beta=0.25 yields no gain over beta=0.0 at 1,024 tokens (-1.07 pp on MATH-500, two-level 95% CI [-4.20, +2.07] pp; -0.16 pp on Val210; -2.08 pp on Ext240; 2x2 interaction -1.80 pp, [-6.93, +3.47] pp); (2) added retained token-512 prefix extractions (gt512_prefix_audit in training_records.json and PASS 3) for all 558 rollouts >512 tokens across Arms 12 and 13, verifying that 87/90 (96.7%) in Arm 12 and 107/118 (90.7%) in Arm 13 of >512-token correct completions had R_512=0 at token 512; (3) updated branch-category counts in Section 4.2 to include Arm 13: (32, 167, 1), (24, 176, 0), and (20, 177, 3); (4) added question-clustered 95% bootstrap CIs alongside two-level CIs in Table 2B; and (5) compacted the training ledger so supplement uncompressed size is ~1.65 MB (well under the 2,000,000 byte limit).",
